{"header":{"numFound":10,"maxScore":20.832834,"queryTime":500,"page":1,"pageSize":30},"results":[{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::8474157d13192953e0e966c6b926b1aa","fullName":"Karol Kulinski","name":"Karol","surname":"Kulinski","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-5403-6629"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Fernando Aguado Gonzalo","name":"Fernando","surname":"Aguado Gonzalo","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Laura Bromboszcz","name":"Laura","surname":"Bromboszcz","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Magdalena Diak","name":"Magdalena","surname":"Diak","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Katarzyna Koziorowska-Makuch","name":"Katarzyna","surname":"Koziorowska-Makuch","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::951c2952bb05d895bd23d5f0b023eb0c","fullName":"Przemyslaw Makuch","name":"Przemyslaw","surname":"Makuch","rank":6,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-9132-1990"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::c079751c8691e0ba48da6b1366a98f2c","fullName":"Izabela Palka","name":"Izabela","surname":"Palka","rank":7,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6705-0721"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Piotr Prusinski","name":"Piotr","surname":"Prusinski","rank":8,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Seyed Reza Saghravani","name":"Seyed Reza","surname":"Saghravani","rank":9,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Beata Szymczycha","name":"Beata","surname":"Szymczycha","rank":10,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Aleksandra Winogradow","name":"Aleksandra","surname":"Winogradow","rank":11,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"13. Climate action"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"14. Life underwater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0105 earth and related environmental sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Climate-related changes in total alkalinity as a key to understanding ocean acidification in the coastal zone","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Rising CO2 concentrations in the atmosphere have a multidimensional influence on marine ecosystems. Through amplifying the greenhouse effect they lead to seawater temperature increase, which initiates cascade changes in the environment. In addition to this climatic pathway, increasing atmospheric CO2 concentrations cause also an overall increase of CO2 concentrations in surface seawater and, consequently, a pH decrease &amp;#8211; a mechanism called Ocean Acidification (OA). OA is already fairly well understood and traceable in the open ocean waters, where large-scale projects and actions supply an enormous amount of observations and experimental data and where the magnitude of OA is to a large extent thermodynamically consistent with the increase in atmospheric pCO2. In the coastal and shelf seas, OA is still a considerably understudied phenomenon despite their high socio-economic importance and potentially great vulnerability of these regions to acidification due to often lower salinity and corresponding lower buffer capacity of waters as compared to open ocean.In the present study, we underline the importance of total alkalinity (TA) as the key factor shaping the OA dynamics and pH fields in the coastal and shelf seas. The extensive research performed in 2018-2022 extended from the brackish Baltic Sea through the open waters of the eastern Fram Strait to the Spitsbergen fjords affected by the high inflow of meltwaters. It revealed extremely high variability in the marine CO2 system structure and significantly different influences of freshwater input in the investigated regions. The observed overall spatial and temporal (seasonal) variability in TA extended in the broad range between &lt;350 and 4,320 &amp;#181;mol kg-1. This makes TA a fundamental variable for studying the large-scale pH and pCO2 changes and forecasting the development of OA in the coastal zone in the future high-CO2 world. This large-scale study can be considered as the reference for future OA research in the investigated regions and simultaneously calls for action to include TA in the routinely observed parameters in the coastal waters.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2023-05-15","publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":null,"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::abc97d5a5b1be5b939de7a6f25c10e5a","originalIds":["10.5194/egusphere-egu23-16078","50|doiboost____|abc97d5a5b1be5b939de7a6f25c10e5a"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5194/egusphere-egu23-16078"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":1.6835128E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Polish Academy of Sciences","acronym":"PAN","id":"openorgs____::f541cd098bd22df66e81d8b34a7238c2","pids":[{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"893139"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000119580162"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/01dr6c206"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q651690"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100004382"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.413454.3"}],"countries":[{"code":"PL","label":"Poland"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.english.pan.pl/"},{"legalName":"Institute of Oceanology","acronym":"IO PAN","id":"openorgs____::ded5d6da4760b427ebebddb8cebb55ff","pids":[{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999488971"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000404068707"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.425054.2"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/03mp6cc45"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q4201640"},{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"PL1115"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q4201640"}],"countries":[{"code":"PL","label":"Poland"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.iopan.gda.pl/index.html"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5194/egusphere-egu23-16078"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-egu23-16078"],"publicationDate":"2023-05-15","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Raven, John A.","name":"John A.","surname":"Raven","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Gobler, Christopher J.","name":"Christopher J.","surname":"Gobler","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::ddf999cfb2e111479f070aaea2b134d2","fullName":"Hansen, Per Juel","name":"Per Juel","surname":"Hansen","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-0228-9621"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":"hybrid","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":[{"code":"GB","label":"United Kingdom","provenance":null},{"code":"DK","label":"Denmark","provenance":null}],"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0301 basic medicine"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Inorganic carbon"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"name=Aquatic Science"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"550"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Harmful Algal Bloom"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"/dk/atira/pure/subjectarea/asjc/1100/1110"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"03 medical and health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Harmful algae"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seawater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"14. Life underwater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Adaptation"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Ecosystem"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0303 health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Algal toxins"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Global warming"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Ocean acidification"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"500"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Eutrophication"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon Dioxide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Hydrogen-Ion Concentration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"15. Life on land"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"6. Clean water"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Experimental evolution"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"13. Climate action"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"/dk/atira/pure/subjectarea/asjc/1100/1104"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"name=Plant Science"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Acclimation"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Dynamic CO2 and pH levels in coastal, estuarine, and inland waters: Theoretical and observed effects on harmful algal blooms","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Rising concentrations of atmospheric CO2 results in higher equilibrium concentrations of dissolved CO2 in natural waters, with corresponding increases in hydrogen ion and bicarbonate concentrations and decreases in hydroxyl ion and carbonate concentrations. Superimposed on these climate change effects is the dynamic nature of carbon cycling in coastal zones, which can lead to seasonal and diel changes in pH and CO2 concentrations that can exceed changes expected for open ocean ecosystems by the end of the century. Among harmful algae, i.e. some species and/or strains of Cyanobacteria, Dinophyceae, Prymnesiophyceae, Bacillariophyceae, and Ulvophyceae, the occurrence of a CO2 concentrating mechanisms (CCMs) is the most frequent mechanism of inorganic carbon acquisition in natural waters in equilibrium with the present atmosphere (400 μmol CO2  mol-1 total gas), with varying phenotypic modification of the CCM. No data on CCMs are available for Raphidophyceae or the brown tide Pelagophyceae. Several HAB species and/or strains respond to increased CO2 concentrations with increases in growth rate and/or cellular toxin content, however, others are unaffected. Beyond the effects of altered C concentrations and speciation on HABs, changes in pH in natural waters are likely to have profound effects on algal physiology. This review outlines the implications of changes in inorganic cycling for HABs in coastal zones, and reviews the knowns and unknowns with regard to how HABs can be expected to ocean acidification. We further point to the large regions of uncertainty with regard to this evolving field."],"publicationDate":"2020-01-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Raven , J A , Gobler , C J & Hansen , P J 2020 , ' Dynamic CO 2 and pH levels in coastal, estuarine, and inland waters : theoretical and observed effects on harmful algal blooms ' , Harmful Algae , vol. 91 , 101594 . https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hal.2019.03.012"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Harmful Algae","issnPrinted":"1568-9883","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"101594","vol":"91","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::f42b795bd63678d04687a58b470a0492","originalIds":["S1568988319300381","10.1016/j.hal.2019.03.012","50|doiboost____|f42b795bd63678d04687a58b470a0492","32057340","2930362719","50|od______2751::f7153024b825143c22e16b7858e3ac27","oai:pure.atira.dk:publications/6a1fbb82-90bf-42a0-9c64-3b9b72b05d59","50|base_oa_____::96eab0fc7bbe85c685c730c8cc742536","ftunivdundeepure:oai:discovery.dundee.ac.uk:publications/3dba595b-c22b-4d6f-872d-34a889471da8","50|base_oa_____::e26cd19b0b683ffe46225fc65bfafa91","ftcopenhagenunip:oai:pure.atira.dk:publications/6a1fbb82-90bf-42a0-9c64-3b9b72b05d59"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.hal.2019.03.012"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"32057340"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":155.0,"influence":5.4510605E-9,"popularity":9.696464E-8,"impulse":75.0,"citationClass":"C3","influenceClass":"C4","impulseClass":"C3","popularityClass":"C3"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"University of Western Australia","acronym":"UWA","id":"openorgs____::017deff5d229f037baa3f5206fda08e2","pids":[{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100004511"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/047272k79"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100001801"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100001174"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1517021"},{"scheme":"GRID","value