ationDate":"2024-10-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::00f0daec9ef6ecfa16d5915fba4dc271","value":"The Science of The Total Environment"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"38889822"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2024.174006"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38889822"],"publicationDate":"2024-07-06","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::9f774f02c3d138f2264d216cf002f3cb","fullName":"Ernesto Villarino","name":"Ernesto","surname":"Villarino","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-1096-261x"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Dorcas Akua Essel","name":"Dorcas Akua","surname":"Essel","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Leire Citores","name":"Leire","surname":"Citores","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::f01b1dee2b666650626a8b7fa984ea10","fullName":"Joana Larreta","name":"Joana","surname":"Larreta","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-8276-9232"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::d70328015b57781e975c5f8a78c98b86","fullName":"Ander Lopez","name":"Ander","surname":"Lopez","rank":5,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6431-0495"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::7ca5662d2917eff0540120c7f6e9b4d8","fullName":"Angel Borja","name":"Angel","surname":"Borja","rank":6,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-1601-2025"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::ce0d8bff27ee26c476f7a18dc2bf7c4a","fullName":"Susana Flecha","name":"Susana","surname":"Flecha","rank":7,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-2826-5820"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Manuel González","name":"Manuel","surname":"González","rank":8,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Luis Cuesta","name":"Luis","surname":"Cuesta","rank":9,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Dorleta Orue-Echevarria","name":"Dorleta","surname":"Orue-Echevarria","rank":10,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Xabier Esteban","name":"Xabier","surname":"Esteban","rank":11,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Guillem Chust","name":"Guillem","surname":"Chust","rank":12,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":[{"code":"ES","label":"Spain","provenance":null}],"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0105 earth and related environmental sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Long-term pH trends across depth in coastal areas of the southeastern Bay of Biscay","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Increased CO2 concentrations in the atmosphere have triggered ocean acidification over the past decades in the global ocean. However, regional efforts of pH monitoring across the southern Bay of Biscay's Basque coast remain elusive, with only a few short-term studies limited to the ocean's surface. Here we examine pH trends over time across the Basque coast using 21733 observations of long-term data collected during 2002–2022 with quarterly CTD casts from surface down to 100 m at three coastal sites. Results revealed significant pH decreases over time in all depth layers (0.5–100 m) at the three coastal sites (0.022–0.041 units decade−1), presumably driven by the global increase of atmospheric CO2. Across depth, observed pH trends also showed significantly higher ocean acidification rates with depth. Seasonally, observed pH changes ranged from wintertime highs of 8.18 ± 0.07 to summertime lows of 8.14 ± 0.05, with a mean seasonal amplitude of about ∼0.04 pH units. The observed pH seasonality and vertical patterns appeared to be tied to the combined effect of environmental factors alongside the development of the thermocline as well as to differences in the biological activity across the water column. Taken together, these findings highlight the importance of pH monitoring in coastal areas and warn on the effect of ocean acidification on marine ecosystems and the services they provide to society.","This study has been supported by Urban Klima 2050 – LIFE 18 IPC 000001 funded by the European Union's LIFE programme. The data used here were obtained from the Basque Water Agency (URA) through the project “Network for monitoring the ecological and chemical status of transitional and coastal waters of the Basque coast”, in partnership organized with AZTI. We thank laboratory technicians and at-sea sampling crew and divers from AZTI for their help. We also thank Igor Granado for technical help in R. This paper is contribution 1277 from AZTI, Marine Research, Basque Research and Technology Alliance (BRTA).","[Data availability] The code that supports the findings of this study as well as part of the data is available in a public repository as well as in Borja et al. 2025. https://gitlab.azti.es/ErnestoVillarino/ph_basque_waters","Peer reviewed"],"publicationDate":"2025-10-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","reponame:Digital.CSIC. Repositorio Institucional del CSIC","instname:Consejo Superior de Investigaciones Científicas (CSIC)"],"formats":null,"contributors":["European Commission","Agencia Vasca del Agua","AZTI-Tecnalia","Basque Research and Technology Alliance","Villarino, Ernesto [0000-0003-1096-261X]","Consejo Superior de Investigaciones Científicas [https://ror.org/02gfc7t72]"],"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_